fix(tests): [FIX-20260623-082] Fix 2 timing-sensitive dedup tests via time.monotonic mock

[Ω-Routing: Scene A → #9 → #8 → #12(L2) → #6 → #5 → #1 → #7]

Causal Chain:
  L1 (symptoms): test_live_alert_hub.py 2 dedup tests FAIL with exit code 1
  in CI full suite, but PASS in isolation — timing-dependent + global-state
  contamination from test_execution_queue.py monkeypatch.setattr("time.monotonic").
  L2 (root cause): time.sleep(0.01) + manual _DEDUP_WINDOW=0.001 override
  vulnerable to both global monkeypatch contamination and Windows timer
  resolution jitter under load (2450+ tests).

test_live_alert_hub.py::TestDedupOrPass had 2 tests that relied on
time.sleep(0.01) to expire a 1ms dedup window:
- test_duplicate_after_window_passes
- test_dedup_with_aggregated_count_on_window_exit

On loaded CI runners (2450+ tests), time.monotonic() can be contaminated by
monkeypatch.setattr("time.monotonic", lambda: 100.0) from
test_execution_queue.py, causing the dedup window to never expire.
This produced 2 FAILs and exit code 1 in CI.

Fix: replace time.sleep(0.01) + manual _DEDUP_WINDOW=0.001 override with
patch.object(time, "monotonic", return_value=time.monotonic() + 61.0) —
explicitly fast-forwards past the 60s default dedup window, eliminating
all timing and global-state dependencies.

Root Cause Layer: L2 — timing-dependent tests susceptible to global
monkeypatch contamination from unrelated test modules.

4D Gate: Stability↑ (no more flaky failures from timing/monkeypatch)
Repairability↑ (explicit mock makes test intent obvious)
Decoupling→ Iterability→
